anonical","teacher_models":["claude-fable-5-1"],"explanation":"The `dividers` helper fails here because the 6x6 reference panel breaks the regular grid of 4-lines (its interior lacks a divider row/col), so I'll locate things as objects instead: with the frame colour 4 as background, the big 6x6 multicolour block (size 36) is the legend, and every 3x3 multicolour block (size 9) is a candidate panel.\n\n**Rule.** The 6x6 block is a 3x3 motif scaled 2x in the \"special\" colour (6, 8 or 3). Downsample it by taking every second cell to get a 3x3 boolean motif. For every 3x3 panel of 0/1 cells, if all motif cells are 1 in the panel (extra 1s allowed — e.g. pair 1's panel at (12,0) is almost all 1s and still matches), recolour exactly the motif cells to the special colour; all other panels stay unchanged.\n\nCheck against the pairs: pair 1 motif `001/110/010` matches panels at (0,0), (12,0), (12,16) → 12 cells become 6; pair 2 motif `101/010/000` matches (0,12), (4,8) → 6 cells become 8; pair 3 motif is the diagonal → matches (0,0), (4,4), (4,12), (16,12) → 12 cells become 3. Those are exactly the changed-cell lists in the fact sheet.\n\nTest: the legend is the 7 block at rows 1–6, cols 16–21; downsampling gives `001/111/100`; each 3x3 panel whose 1s cover that motif gets those cells painted 7.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    out = g.copy()\n    frame = 4  # frame colour is 4 in every pair\n    objs = objects(g, bg=frame, multicolour=True)\n    big = [o for o in objs if o[\"size\"] == 36 and o[\"box\"][2]-o[\"box\"][0] == 5 and o[\"box\"][3]-o[\"box\"][1] == 5][0]\n    y0, x0, y1, x1 = big[\"box\"]\n    bc = crop(g, y0, x0, y1, x1)\n    special = [c for c in np.unique(bc) if c != 0 and c != frame][0]\n    pat = (bc[::2, ::2] == special)  # 3x3 motif\n    emit(out, \"Legend found: the 6x6 block is a 3x3 motif scaled 2x in colour %d; downsampled motif identified\" % special)\n    small = [o for o in objs if o[\"size\"] == 9 and o[\"box\"][2]-o[\"box\"][0] == 2 and o[\"box\"][3]-o[\"box\"][1] == 2]\n    for o in small:\n        a, b, c, d = o[\"box\"]\n        sub = g[a:c+1, b:d+1]\n        if np.all(sub[pat] == 1):\n            out[a:c+1, b:d+1][pat] = special\n            emit(out, \"Panel at rows %d-%d cols %d-%d contains the motif in its 1-cells: recolour the motif cells to %d\" % (a, c, b, d, special))\n    emit(out, \"All panels checked; final result\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"panels":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The `dividers` helper fails here because the 6x6 reference panel breaks the regular grid of 4-lines (its interior lacks a divider row/col), so I'll locate things as objects instead: with the frame colour 4 as background, the big 6x6 multicolour block (size 36) is the legend, and every 3x3 multicolour block (size 9) is a candidate panel."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"For every 3x3 panel of 0/1 cells, if all motif cells are 1 in the panel (extra 1s allowed — e.g. pair 1's panel at (12,0) is almost all 1s and still matches), recolour exactly the motif cells to the special colour; all other panels stay unchanged."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Check against the pairs: pair 1 motif `001/110/010` matches panels at (0,0), (12,0), (12,16) → 12 cells become 6; pair 2 motif `101/010/000` matches (0,12), (4,8) → 6 cells become 8; pair 3 motif is the diagonal → matches (0,0), (4,4), (4,12), (16,12) → 12 cells become 3."}],"legend":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"ects instead: with the frame colour 4 as background, the big 6x6 multicolour block (size 36) is the legend, and every 3x3 multicolour block (size 9) is a candidate panel."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Test: the legend is the 7 block at rows 1–6, cols 16–21; downsampling gives `001/111/100`; each 3x3 panel whose 1s cover that motif gets those cells painted 7."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Legend found: the 6x6 block is a 3x3 motif scaled 2x in colour 6; downsampled motif identified"}],"recolour":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"in the panel (extra 1s allowed — e.g. pair 1's panel at (12,0) is almost all 1s and still matches), recolour exactly the motif cells to the special colour; all other panels stay unchanged."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Panel at rows 0-2 cols 0-2 contains the motif in its 1-cells: recolour the motif cells to 6"},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Panel at rows 12-14 cols 0-2 contains the motif in its 1-cells: recolour the motif cells to 6"}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Rule.** The 6x6 block is a 3x3 motif scaled 2x in the \"special\" colour (6, 8 or 3)."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Downsample it by taking every second cell to get a 3x3 boolean motif."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"For every 3x3 panel of 0/1 cells, if all motif cells are 1 in the panel (extra 1s allowed — e.g. pair 1's panel at (12,0) is almost all 1s and still matches), recolour exactly the motif cells to the special colour; all other panels stay unchanged."}],"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"dividers` helper fails here because the 6x6 reference panel breaks the regular grid of 4-lines (its interior lacks a divider row/col), so I'll locate things as objects instead: with the frame colour 4 as background, the big 6x6 multicolour block (size 36) is the legend, and every 3x3 multicolour block (size 9) is a candidate panel."}],"boolean":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Downsample it by taking every second cell to get a 3x3 boolean motif."}],"scale":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Rule.** The 6x6 block is a 3x3 motif scaled 2x in the \"special\" colour (6, 8 or 3)."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Legend found: the 6x6 block is a 3x3 motif scaled 2x in colour 6; downsampled motif identified"},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Legend found: the 6x6 block is a 3x3 motif scaled 2x in colour 8; downsample